-- hand-authored, no-combat traverse). That is superseded here -- see
-- Content/Worlds/EtherealScape.luau and docs/biomes/ETHEREAL_SCAPE.md's header
-- for the reasoning. This is a NEW chunk kit, first pass: geometrically
-- validated (30/30 pieces pass footprint/height/tri-budget checks), not yet
-- uploaded or walked in Studio -- the same status Verdant Valley's 30-piece
-- kit started at.
--
-- Round, organic sky-temple islands above the cloud deck. 30 pieces, built
-- from five axes (Shape/Floor/Edge/Keel/Landmark) so no two read alike.
--
-- CONNECTION VOCABULARY -- decided before modelling, per CHUNK_AUTHORING.md
-- "Starting a different world". Deliberately disjoint from Sky Citadel's
-- SKYWAY/ASCENT and Verdant Valley's PATH/WIDE; a test asserts every world's
-- kind set is disjoint from every other's.
--   SPAN       connective. A 44-stud causeway, walk plane at the origin.
--   COMMUNION  arena-only. A 64-stud ceremonial approach. Only the two Temple
--              Gates offer one, so a gate precedes the Sanctum on every seed.
--
-- Sockets: Facing is degrees, 0 = -Z (north), 90 = +X (east), 180 = +Z
-- (south), 270 = -X (west). Offsets are local to the piece, before rotation --
-- same convention as Sky Citadel and Verdant Valley.
--
-- SIZE: 256 x 256 x 256 for every piece except the Sanctum (320 x 320 x 256).
-- The generator pins the box with four 0.3-stud edge pins at z = -96 and one
-- landmark per piece reaching +160. The walk plane sits 32 studs below the
-- box centre for the 256-piece set, same as Sky Citadel's kit.
local WIDTH = { SPAN = 44, COMMUNION = 64 }

local function socket(id: string, kind: string, x: number, z: number, facing: number)
	return {
		Id = id,
		Kind = kind,
		OffsetX = x,
		OffsetY = 0,
		OffsetZ = z,
		Facing = facing,
		Width = WIDTH[kind],
	}
end

